mantle rm335
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_una_thackeray
title the landing game
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk deals_imaginary_cards_to_pairs_of_passing_boots
likes honey_cakes cards new_boots autumn_wind
dislikes cold_tea flies
fears an_empty_seat_on_a_windy_day
hopes one_good_hand_before_the_kettle_cools
topics pastimes +0.6 smalltalk +0.4 weather +0.4 food +0.2
styles comfort=seat gossip=dry refuse=blunt tease=mild
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# deals imaginary cards to passing pairs of boots and takes the long stairs briskly whenever the view from one landing grows dull.

words
oath! = Two left boots | Fold the landing
saying! = The stair deals for free | No boot wins by standing still
deck = my worn pack | the little deck
bootpair = a smart pair | two dusty boots
heel = the square heel | that worn heel
card = the last card | a bent card
stamp = a hollow tread | a solid stamp
seat = my broad perch | the sheltered seat
cup = the heavy cup | a chipped mug
cake = a honey morsel | the sticky square
brim = a tea rim | a wet circle
pip = a faded pip | one little dot
cloth = the grey wrap | a folded square
gust = an autumn gust | a hard crosswind

any
opinion houses against 1 : I'd play any House that had to show its cards by rules common to the table.
opinion merchants against 1 : A seller ought to put the price on the visible side of the card.
opinion sump for 1 : The low streets make good use of steps for which the builders imagined only walking.
opinion dole for 2 : Empty paws oughtn't to exclude a wolf from dinner. It's quite a good reason to offer one.
opinion watch against 1 : A pair of official boots in a hurry wins no special points in my game.
opinion road for 1 : There's no admission fee for watching folk come and go. I appreciate a well-priced amusement.

grown
line greet : Hello. You've drawn a seat beside the dealer. | Take a seat. We're between deals.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new pair enters. Welcome. | First meeting, so I'll let the boots introduce themselves.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The first few pairs have a brisk look. | New deal for the day, then.
line greet.return : Hello back. You have both my eyes now. | I heard you on the turn before you spoke.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Familiar tread. You're entitled to the good edge of the seat. | Here's somebody worth folding a card for.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late hello. Even heels change their note after dark. | You've turned up in the quiet hand.
line again.open : A return appearance counts double on my stair. | We seem to have shuffled into company again.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here. A rather fine pair has entered play. | Come watch while the lane deals us another.
line farewell : Keep your soles under you and your cards dry. | May your next seat have a back to it.
line farewell.return : I'll call that a fair withdrawal. Goodbye. | Away before the next hand claims you.
line react.news : I've put the pack down. Let's hear it. | Deal the actual news face up.
line react.news.new : None of that had turned up in my hand. | The stair neglected to deliver that report.
line react.news.known : Heard that one before the tea got cold. | Yes. The first telling sounded much the same.
line react.news.doubt : That's a lot of talk on one small card. | I wouldn't stake my last decent seat on it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : You can sit the next few hands out here with me. | That news would leave the liveliest boots dragging.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : I'd call that the best turn in an otherwise ordinary hand. | Something worth letting the tea cool to hear.
line ask.how : What kind of hand has the day dealt you? | Did you find a perch worth the climb?
line answer.how : Still holding a card or two. One even looks promising. | Quite still for a wolf with so many opinions about feet.
line decline : I'd be playing a hand I haven't got if I agreed. | That's further than these boots are committed to going today.
line accept_decline : Then I'll deal round the empty place. | Fair answer. I haven't lost a thing by asking.
line preclose : I'll shift my seat before I begin to take root. | A fresh deal somewhere else would suit me.
line accept_preclose : No charge for leaving the game early. | You can go without showing the rest of your hand.
line thank : You've kept my tea warm and my temper level. Thanks. | I owe you the pick of the next seat.
line deflect_thanks : I was sitting with a perfectly spare paw. | Hardly an undertaking to slide the pack along.
line sympathise : Rest here without joining the game if you like. | Bad hands take time to set down too.
line reassure : This hand's nearly over. We'll have another look then. | I can keep you company till the tea warms.
line ack : My tally agrees with yours. | That card fits the space exactly.
line give.advice : Choose the seat before pouring the tea. | Don't judge the whole walk by a particularly loud heel.

scene bootdeal
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My boots get black cards. Passing boots earn red ones. | I can play without a pack if folk keep coming up the stair.
b : How does a pair earn points? | And who gets to be dealer?
a : A matched pace wins one. A squeaking sole loses it. The rules are extremely respectable. | Me. I invented the game to suit a wolf sitting down.

scene oddpair
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two steps in one make an excellent way to change where I'm sitting. | I hurry between good seats so I can take my time once there.
b : You count sitting as an activity? | Why hurry if you're only going to sit?
a : Watch me. I've brought it to a moderately exact science. | I'd miss half the boots if I spent my whole day on the staircase.

scene deckedge
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a bent card upside down in the pack before I forget where it lies. | A marked corner will tell a player too much without being asked.
b : Isn't that still a mark? | Why keep it in the pack then?
a : Yes, which is why I show it round the table ahead of the deal. | Because the deck's short without it. Knowing equally little is the next best plan.

scene honeycut
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Divide the cake before dealing. Sticky cards don't separate on demand. | I want my fingers clean until the last card's on the board.
b : Can a game really wait for cake? | And your cake while you play?
a : A cake can. A sticky deal is a long-lasting mistake. | Set aside in sight. My interest in the result will be wonderfully keen.

scene teaclock
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have one reliable clock for a game. If the tea goes cold we've talked too long. | Cold tea counts as a defeat however well I played.
b : Drink it halfway through then. | You blame the cards for that?
a : Sensible suggestion. Rather spoils my excuse when the cards are poor. | I blame my inability to observe the tea and the hand simultaneously.

scene pastboots
when topic=home self.quarter=works
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Works the rush at a shift change makes my boot game unplayably quick. | My best watching hour sits between shifts in the Works.
b : Too many feet to count? | What's left to see in between?
a : A whole pack's worth arrives at once. I prefer some suspense. | The late ones. More individuality in a wolf who has already missed the bell.

scene poorseat
when topic=prices self.wealth=destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've enough coin for very little indulgence. Sitting down is still priced admirably. | New boots appeal to me especially at the moment I can't pay for them.
b : Do you mind somebody else's fine pair? | Does the game make that better?
a : I give it an imaginary good card. Costs less than leather treatment. | It makes an afternoon more interesting. For a pair of boots I'd still need a cobbler.

scene solehope
when topic=dreams self.likes=new_boots
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to enter my own new boots in the game one day. | A pair with clean heels would represent me very handsomely.
b : Who'd award the points? | Would you automatically win?
a : I'd ask somebody to sit in my place. I can't inspect the backs of my own heels very well. | Only if the dealer showed remarkable good taste.

scene winddeck
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn wind is a very enthusiastic extra player. | A stiff breeze deals from the bottom, the top and the middle all at once.
b : Does it play fair? | What keeps the cards on the table?
a : It shows every card to everybody. I'd call that excessive fairness. | One paw on the pack. The other occupied with a cup. A game for the well-organised.

scene flygame
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly can make a quite unearned black spot on a low card. | I count spots only after they've stopped walking.
b : What if the fly changes the result? | Would you let it join?
a : It has no entry fee. I shall disqualify it on a technicality. | Only if it agreed to go somewhere else for cake. I don't share on those terms.

scene childlook
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd invite #self.child# to make up another rule for my boot game. | There's always room by my seat for #self.child#.
b : Even a rule you don't like? | Does the game need two?
a : Especially one I don't like. Gives me a decent grievance to entertain me. | No. The company improves a pastime already much improved by being free.

scene ownwork
when topic=work self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Observation isn't a wage-paying trade in my experience. | I watch the passing day quite carefully without charging it for the service.
b : What does your observation earn? | A disappointing arrangement?
a : A view and an occasional conversation. Neither boils a pot, but both matter. | I'd accept a fee, certainly. Till then at least I can set my own hours.

scene lettervine
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've tried drawing vineyard rows as a pattern on a blank card. | A little account of a hillside set me thinking about a different sort of pack.
b : Would the vines be trumps? | What did the first card look like?
a : If I dealt there, perhaps. On a stair I favour boots. | Two green rows round a purple spot. Good enough to suggest grapes to a hungry player.

scene gossipseat
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A seated wolf sees some remarkable boots. That's no great authority on the wearers. | I can judge a scrape of leather and still know nothing of a quarrel.
b : You'd take no guesses? | You must overhear a lot.
a : About the boots, certainly. Beyond the ankle my information gets thin. | I can fold a card and stop listening. It's a courtesy quite within my reach.

scene drawtimes
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the cupboard runs bare I don't risk anything on a hand. | A tight week makes a fine argument for counting boots instead of coppers.
b : A game for nothing, then? | What do you win?
a : For an hour's amusement. That's a thing, even if it won't go into the pot. | A good story about a squeaking heel. You could do worse for no stake.

scene praybench
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A chapel bench is one place I give the boots a complete rest. | There are moments I'd rather see the floor empty and the door quiet.
b : No cards in chapel? | Even silence gets its turn?
a : I keep them wrapped. I've another reason for sitting there. | Yes. I rather like sitting with the Bright One without keeping score.

scene nixtalk
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At night the boot game goes entirely by sound. | I can hear an especially hollow heel from quite a distance when the lane's quiet.
b : Can you tell which suit? | You'd know who was coming?
a : Cloth soles play a silent suit. They're the bane of my late game. | No. Can hear a heel, can't read a name off the echoes.

scene wetcards
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Lift the cards before wiping a wet bench. | A card laid face down on a damp board develops a lasting friendship.
b : Would a dry cloth save it? | Will it come off whole?
a : If you use the cloth first, certainly. Order is important. | Very slowly. I've no wish to leave the face of a card on a public seat.

grown

story doubledeal [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I saw a splendid clean pair come by twice and gave the pair two high cards. Came past a third time looking a little less impressive.
  : I'd been awarding points to the same circuit of a puddle.
  b : Did you subtract them?
  : Certainly not. Three clean crossings round that patch deserved every point.

story teaace [topic=food|memories]
  : I dealt a hand on a cloth beside my tea and couldn't find one card when the game ended.
  : Lifted the mug and found the missing card underneath. The circle on it was remarkably neat.
  b : Could you play with it again?
  : It has a new rank. Highest tea cup beats any card made thirsty enough to challenge it.

story windseat [topic=weather|memories]
  : I carried a folded card to a sheltered seat because the wind had already taken one off the original bench.
  : Found the missing card waiting there ahead of me.
  b : A better judge of shelter than you?
  : Better informed. It had been taken on a free tour of the available draughts.

rule @heel
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Square heel, low note. That pair goes in the black pile. | Two clean soles. An excellent opening bid.

rule @wind
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the wind shuffle its own pack! | Put the mug on the cloth before the whole game sets sail.

rule @tea
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Still steaming round the rim. I've another hand in me. | A tepid cup means the game has gone into extra time.

rule @honey
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sticky fingers can wait till the cards are counted. | Just a corner of cake and I'll have a clean paw again.

dlg resident.hub : I've a vacant seat and a game that can spare its dealer. Speak freely.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I shall have to invent a new card for all these return appearances.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : In this quiet even distant cards make themselves heard.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There's a whole unoccupied tread between us. Let's leave it so.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none] : The passing world hasn't employed me, but I keep a pretty good watch on it.
dlg resident.job : Any work that requires noticing little changes in pace is apt to hold my attention.
dlg resident.bye : May your next hand arrive with a warm cup beside it.

graft resident.hub
choice What card do my boots get? -> bootvalue
node bootvalue
say You came up here and stopped of your own accord. That's a high red card for manners, provided you don't ask what it will buy you.
free
choice Could they ever lose the card? -> mendingrule
choice I'll keep the points for manners. -> hub
node mendingrule
say A heel on my toes might cost the whole thing. Apart from that the score stands until I think of a better game. An exceptionally stable arrangement.
choice I'll stand clear of your toes. -> hub
choice I'll play another day. -> bye
